# IRMarket Frontend — Environment

Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and set the deployed addresses. These are required by
`src/lib/wagmi.ts` and `src/lib/market.ts` once the frontend connects to contracts.

## Upstream (A) stack — Monad testnet, PRODUCTION (see docs/design/monoracle-upstream-handoff.md)

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=https://testnet-rpc.monad.xyz
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=10143
NEXT_PUBLIC_MARKET_ADDRESS=0x05475037AE4e0717083737eDAc38590850968E7c
# Upstream Monoracle lazy/implicit settlement (canonical price derived at read time).
NEXT_PUBLIC_ORACLE_ADDRESS=0x0BC36e1ac475AdEF75F102deb1708BE6E45aA16f
# priceBase (NVDA) / quote (HKD)
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_TOKEN=0xda9CF5A68cc2d8EFA5940db4094b6377D389DE17
NEXT_PUBLIC_QUOTE_TOKEN=0x36448Ef080ba5fa251e1a9bd61782786f9e24F04
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAULT_ADDRESS=0x3d52a82a8a79b4Aecc90F37e506a441e0eF908AB
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXPIRY_SECONDS=1800
# Curation (frontend-only registry, per-pair vault model — docs/architecture.md §7):
# comma-separated base tokens the product shows. Empty/absent = show every wrapper market.
# NOTE: SOXX (iShares Semiconductor ETF) joins the curated set once its market is deployed via
# script/deploy-market-stack.js — append its base token to the list below when available.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SELECTED_BASE_TOKENS=0xda9CF5A68cc2d8EFA5940db4094b6377D389DE17
# Optional: a nuthatch nest over the market + oracle above (dixia/IRMarket#1) serves positions
# over full history in one request. Unset, or if the nest cannot vouch for these addresses,
# usePositions scans eth_getLogs as before.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_INDEXER_URL=https://irmarket.89.167.109.4.sslip.io
```

